## P1 to P4: the prefix defect, measured before and after the repair
The independent checks of e14dbee found that the layer silently dropped
the prefix of an archive whose producer records file-absolute offsets,
and that a zip64 archive behind a prefix with an archive-relative locator
was refused. Planning reproduced both against its own build before ruling
(specs/0008-zip-layer.md, the P1 rulings of 2026-09-17). Four fixtures
are built here and run through BOTH binaries, so the defect and the fix
are each a measurement rather than a claim.
The generator is this log's own. It does not use the crate's test
builder: a fixture and the code it tests sharing a parent is how the
original fixture came to encode the implementation's own convention.
Every signature it needs is ASSERTED, not guarded: an earlier attempt at
these fixtures skipped its zip64 patches behind 'if found >= 0' and
